      "id": "claim_c2f6f4b2912b48628b8b14b3e92b28d5",
      "statement": "Both extensions target only regular HTTP/HTTPS pages via isRegularPageUrl; Chrome grants broad host permission at install (no runtime request, hasRegularPageAccess always true), while Safari declares *://*/* as a required permission with no chrome.permissions API, so both hasRegularPageAccess and requestRegularPageAccess always return true and there is no 'regular page access not enabled' state on Safari.",
      "evidence": [
