      "id": "claim_68cd090d902a4250b319b08023a55c59",
      "statement": "Chrome's DownloadAdapter uses chrome.downloads for full download status and numeric downloadId, degrading to not_supported if absent; Safari's SafariDownloadAdapter returns not_supported for status and fire-and-forget downloadFile (opens a new tab, initiated_fire_and_forget, null downloadId). Both share a fetch-based fetchResource with credentials, timeout, base64+SHA256, and AbortError->timeout / TypeError->cors_blocked mapping.",
